<article class="env-lemma" id="07W6">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/07W6">Lemma <span data-tag="07W6">90.19.10</span>.</a> Let $\varphi : \mathcal{F} \to \mathcal{G}$ be a morphism of categories cofibred in groupoids over $\mathcal{C}_\Lambda $ satisfying (RS). Let $x_0 \in \mathop{\mathrm{Ob}}\nolimits (\mathcal{F}(k))$. Then $\varphi $ induces a $k$-linear map $\text{Inf}_{x_0}(\mathcal{F}) \to \text{Inf}_{\varphi (x_0)}(\mathcal{G})$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      It is clear that $\varphi $ induces a morphism from $\mathit{Aut}(x_0) \to \mathit{Aut}(\varphi (x_0))$ which maps the identity to the identity. Hence this follows from the result for tangent spaces, see Lemma <a href="/tag/06IJ" data-tag="06IJ">90.12.4</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>